### Terraform ###
# State describes one machine's own local kind cluster and is not shareable. The lock file is
# deliberately NOT ignored, so provider versions stay pinned across machines.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
# The tehcyx/kind provider writes a kubeconfig named <cluster_name>-config into the Terraform
# working directory as a side effect of creating a cluster -- nothing in main.tf asks for it, and
# it reappears on every apply. It embeds the cluster CA *and a client private key*, so it must
# never be committed. `terraform output kubectl_context` is the supported way in; kind already
# merges the same context into ~/.kube/config.
terraform/*-config
